(Bug #56: `all the numbers from/between ...` names a range, and a range is a
 loop's counter bounds - LANGUAGE.md:262 says ranges are never allocated as
 lists. Every `for each` header that is handed one now runs the range loop,
 where before it kept the range as a list collection and codegen walked the
 accumulator as a list header and segfaulted.

 All three headers that take a collection are covered, in both spellings of
 the phrase: `in`, `from`, and the loop-expansion clause. The plain range
 that none of this changed is the last case, and it is the control: every
 block above it must read the same.)

For each step in all the numbers between 1 and 3,
    print step.

For each step in all the numbers from 1 to 3,
    print step.

For each step from all the numbers between 1 and 3,
    print step.

For each step from all the numbers from 1 to 3,
    print step.

print each step from all the numbers between 1 and 3.

print each step from all the numbers from 1 to 3.

print each step from 1 to 3.
